{
	title: 'SYSTEM.md layout: every line in a section, grouped variables',
	spec: 'All SYSTEM.md text sits in :: sections (Identity, Rules, Tools, Slash commands, Hal notes, READ, BASH, EDIT, Other tools, Images, User notes, Session role, Spawn budget, Session, Local instructions); a section costs only its heading. Nothing the native tool definition says is repeated: Tools keeps only the argument format and the cwd path rule; the cmd description reads TOOL followed by its arguments with examples and the HELP <TOOL> hint. BASH says to avoid rm -rf $VAR (example /tmp/hal-$session_id-benchmark/), to use the /tmp/hal-$session_id- prefix for scratch files, and that long-running commands use background with a timeout. Interactive sessions are told to start every BASH and EDIT with a /* purpose */ comment, with an example (also extras/multiedit.ts); calls without one stay accepted. Spawn budget renders only when slots are not 0: interactive non-subagent sessions spawn only when the user approves; subagents and non-interactive sessions get the guidance that agent-agent communication loses information. Template variables are grouped: date; session_id, session_cwd, session_model, session_dir, session_interactive, session_autoclose; hal_dir, hal_home, hal_source, hal_web_url; subagent, subagent_owner, subagent_slots; fork, fork_parent; user_notes, other_tools, agents. The header comment states SYSTEM.md is the complete system prompt and documents the AGENTS.md loading policy before $agents.',
